#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a83c4e86-5ecb-5ab8-ac53-ef7e6fcfb22d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347046} {:answer/id #uuid "52e2d59b-a700-5f5b-8984-5ce7f5af8b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347047} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb5f02b-69a0-50cc-a1cd-2961079a75b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347048} {:answer/id #uuid "9473b6c2-2d87-5f21-86fa-1cfa5671c801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347049} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb74918-959c-5b65-9767-c73a257cca8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9473b6c2-2d87-5f21-86fa-1cfa5671c801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347049} :answer-field/id #uuid "3082440f-90a7-5f00-948f-05dc52bfa82f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02d64a49-09f3-54fa-aded-dbe6a0beb5fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161712" :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,0\\le y\\le xz}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=xz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}[{\\int }_{0}^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}{\\int }_{0}^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=(0)+(2x)=2x.\n$$"}]}
